  "verbalization": "Perphenazine, a phenothiazine compound, is consistently linked to Calm3 through a shared ontological pathway. The evidence suggests that Perphenazine, as part of the phenothiazine class, binds to Calm3 via a common ancestor in the phenothiazine family. This binding is supported by multiple paths, with the lowest common ancestor of Perphenazine and Promethazine being the phenothiazines, which in turn bind to Calm3. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target, Calm3, underscores a potential mechanism where phenothiazines, through their shared pharmacological profile, exert effects on Calm3. The integration of these paths highlights a recurring mechanism of interaction between phenothiazines and Calm3, likely through a direct or indirect binding mechanism. The evidence also suggests that Perphenazine may influence Calm3 through a pathway involving other agents, such as N-alkylpiperazines or antipsychotic agents, further supporting a broader pharmacological context. The integration of these findings provides a concise explanation for the relationship between Perphenazine and Calm3, emphasizing the role of phenothiazines in modulating Calm3 through shared biological mechanisms.",
